    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d502">

                <pb facs="0478" n="466" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg466"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.91/11–344</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Under Secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stettinius</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-11-03">November 3, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Dr. Daftary, the Iranian Chargé d’Affaires, called this afternoon at his
                    request.</p>
                <pb facs="0479" n="467" xml:id="pg467"/>
                <p>He stated that he had been instruction [<hi rendition="#italic">instructed</hi>]
                    to call upon me immediately to advise me of the deplorable relations between
                    Iran and the Soviet Union. He said that the Russians captured many Iranian
                    troops and police in the northern part of the country, had taken their weapons
                    and ammunition, and that the highways had been cut off and large segments of the
                    population left without water and food. He characterized the situation as most
                    distressing and critical and stated that his Government was appealing to the
                    United States to take a firm position with Russia immediately.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E[<hi rendition="#small-caps">dward</hi>] S[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >tettinius</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
